{"text": "grandmother", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">graundmodre</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">grauntmoder</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">granmoder</i>; equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">grand-</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">mother</i>. Compare French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fr\">grand-m\u00e8re</i>. Superseded earlier <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">eldmother</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">eldermother</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "A mother of someone's parent.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "A female ancestor or progenitor.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["UK", "/\u02c8\u0261\u0279\u00e6n(d)\u02ccm\u028c\u00f0\u0259(r)/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8\u0261\u0279\u00e6n\u02ccm\u028c\u00f0\u0259/"], ["General American", "/\u02c8\u0261\u0279\u00e6n(d)\u02ccm\u028c\u00f0\u025a/"]]}